DERIVED FACT 4: submission routing is public, and it is pinned
========================================================================

  Deep history, not just the sampled window:
    treasury 0.0.10116630         190 token txs across 1 node(s)
      node 0.0.29     190  100.0%   Aberdeen Investments
    counterparty 0.0.10420070     111 token txs across 3 node(s)
      node 0.0.29     109   98.2%   Aberdeen Investments
      node 0.0.7        1    0.9%   Nomura
      node 0.0.10       1    0.9%   

  CONTROL. Is that concentration normal? 100 random recent mainnet txs:
    distinct receiving nodes 28, busiest 7.0% of traffic
    Routing across mainnet is spread over the whole address book.
    So 100 percent on one node is a deliberate pin, not a default.

  The receiving consensus node is a PUBLIC field on every transaction.
  Two things follow. The consensus visibility lever is already production
  practice, so it is not exotic. And it is not confidential: the
  choice of first observer is itself disclosed, permanently.
  fn(nothing in the ten). A new axis, not a new row.

  Stated without allegation, because the structural point does not
  need one: every transaction on this treasury, across five competing
  managers, is handed first to a node operated by one of them.

